# s3-22 desktop wire (applied by the DESKTOP-WIRE task of the wave)

main/host/computer.ts, registerComputerHost(connection, source), after the registerComputerInternalWindows(connection) line:

    registerComputerPixels(connection, { callCore: (method, params) => connection.request(method, params) });

and its import, beside the other computer-* imports:

    import { registerComputerPixels } from './computer-pixels';

HOST_METHOD rows: none (the name HOST_COMPUTER_PIXELS = 'host/computer/pixels' lives in host/computer-pixels.ts, as
HOST_COMPUTER_FOREGROUND_LEASE does in computer-lease.ts).

Optional: `blobChunkBytes: () => <the core's limits.maxBlobPutChunkBytes from initialize>` in the deps object; without it every
chunk is 96 KiB, which is under every core's limit.

Core side: host/computer/pixels is served only on a desktop with this fragment applied; computer_pixels.rs already treats
-32601 as unavailable, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING by this fragment.
